	<body>
		<outline text="/scripting.com/code/pagepark/">
			<outline text="worknotes.md">
				<outline text="#### 11/10/26; 9:29:09 AM by DW">
					<outline text="An app in the default folder now handles every request that falls to that folder, the way an app in a domain’s own folder handles that domain’s requests.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Also an app in the default folder handles every request that falls to it, except Caddy's certificate question, which PagePark answers itself.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="When returning a Markdown doc, include the encoding, the standard for text/markdown requires it.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/9/26; 12:44:28 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Support new feature, a default folder can now specify what cnames it's ready to handle, and we reply to Caddy accordingly. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/3/25; 12:13:13 PM by DW ">
					<outline text="I'm having difficulty with Caddy, it's sending attempts to connect via WebSockets to WordLand. It only handles HTTP.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Added new config value -- flWebsocketsIsError, defaults false. Don't want to break any apps that do handle WS requests. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/15/24; 12:23:14 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Prevented a crashing bug in processResponse.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/5/24; 11:46:02 AM by DW">
					<outline text="I wish there were a way to configure the domains folder, but it isn't there. So I'm using a symlink.">
						<outline text="here's the directory I want to link to">
							<outline text="~/Dropbox/Miami/pagePark/domains">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="and the directory I want to link from">
							<outline text="~/taos/pagepark/domains">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="apparently the command is">
							<outline text="ln -s ~/Dropbox/Miami/pagePark/domains ~/taos/pagepark/domains">
							</outline>
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 1/8/24; 9:38:20 AM by DW">
					<outline text="PagePark now works with specs for news products using JSON in addition to OPML.  ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The data supplied is basically the same, the format is different.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="An &lt;a href=&quot;http://scripting.com/code/newsproducthome/newsscriptingcom2.json&quot;&gt;example&lt;/a&gt; of a JSON-spec. Also it's explained on the &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.feedland.dev/extras.md#json-specified-news-products&quot;&gt;FeedLand docs&lt;/a&gt; site. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&lt;%includeExample (&quot;newsProductGlue2&quot;)%&gt;">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The big difference is that instead of a `urlTemplate` value, there's `urlNewsProductSpec`.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/27/23; 1:05:46 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Running news products for FeedLand. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="We were and still are using filter.js to hook up newsproducts via a PagePark domain. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I wanted to simplify the connecting code and make it part of PagePark.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="To invoke a newsproduct: ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&lt;%includeExample (&quot;newsProductGlue&quot;)%&gt;">
					</outline>
					<outline text="This will change, as we use JSON in place of OPML for templates. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Some of the terminology may change as well.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/2/23; 10:52:58 AM by DW">
					<outline text="We can now serve from private GitHub repos. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="To do so, add an &lt;i&gt;accessToken&lt;/i&gt; value to your &lt;i&gt;githubServeFrom&lt;/i&gt; object in config.json.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="When we get the page text from GitHub that will be in the Authorization header in the request. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="An example of a PagePark &lt;a href=&quot;https://gist.github.com/scripting/3f43bd5b7b5b05dad62214102085c2aa&quot;&gt;config.json file&lt;/a&gt; to access a private repo via the web.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/20/23; 8:53:50 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Another pagepark crash, this time on peabody, very reproducible. If you go to https://this.how/ -- it crashes. Happens in opmltojs package. I'm going to try setting up a local test and see if I can reproduce here. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The problem was in opmltojs package, it the xml parser wasn't returning an error when it wasn't able to parse an OPML file, so I added an extra check for a null value returned, and the crash went away. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Now it's good question why the parser couldn't handle it because it looks to be valid xml, it's the index.opml file for the this.how website. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/15/23; 5:37:20 PM by DW">
					<outline text="if pagepark crashes on a machine that's running caddy, all the apps launch but the ports are already in use, so the keep launching and the machine effectively goes crazy. i found the problem by leaving a console window open, logging pagepark hits, and when the machine went nuts i scrolled back until i found the source. ">
						<outline text="lowerhost = host.toLowerCase ()">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="so i check first if host is undefined and set it to the empty string. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
			</outline>
			<outline text="package.json">
				<outline text="{ ">
					<outline text="&quot;name&quot;: &quot;PagePark&quot;, ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;description&quot;: &quot;A simple Node.js folder-based HTTP server that serves static and dynamic pages for domains.&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;author&quot;: &quot;Dave Winer &lt;dave@scripting.com&gt;&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;version&quot;: &quot;0.9.5&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;scripts&quot;: {">
						<outline text="&quot;start&quot;: &quot;node pagepark.js&quot;">
							<outline text="},">
							</outline>
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;repository&quot;: {">
						<outline text="&quot;type&quot; : &quot;git&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;url&quot; : &quot;https://github.com/scripting/pagePark.git&quot;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="},">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;dependencies&quot; : { ">
						<outline text="&quot;request&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;mime&quot;: &quot;*&quot;," isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;daveopml&quot;: &quot;*&quot;," isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;pagepark&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;opmltojs&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;daveutils&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;daves3&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;davediskspace&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;githubpub&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;pagepark&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;nodejs-websocket&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;require-from-string&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;marked&quot;: &quot;3.0.8&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;child_process&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;forever&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;forever-monitor&quot;: &quot;*&quot;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}, ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;license&quot;: &quot;MIT&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;engines&quot;: {">
						<outline text="&quot;node&quot;: &quot;*&quot;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
			</outline>
			<outline text="pagepark.js">
				<outline text="var myProductName = &quot;PagePark&quot;, myVersion = &quot;0.9.5&quot;; ">
